S={
'common carotid artery':'Runs up the neck <b>with the vagosympathetic trunk</b> in the carotid sheath. It ends by splitting into the internal and external carotids.',
'caudal thyroid artery':'A small artery to the <b>caudal pole of the thyroid</b>, coming up from the brachiocephalic trunk.',
'cranial thyroid artery':'The <b>first branch of the common carotid</b>, to the thyroid gland, larynx and pharynx.',
'medial retropharyngeal lymph node':'The big lymph node <b>dorsal to the pharynx, medial to the mandibular salivary gland</b>, right by the carotid split. It drains the whole head.',
'internal carotid artery':'The small branch at the carotid split that runs to the <b>brain</b> (through the carotid canal to the arterial circle).',
'carotid sinus':'The slight <b>swelling at the start of the internal carotid</b>. It senses blood pressure.',
'external carotid artery':'The big continuation of the common carotid. It supplies the face, tongue and jaws and ends as the <b>maxillary + superficial temporal</b> arteries.',
'superficial temporal artery':'One of the <b>2 terminal branches of the external carotid</b>. It runs up in front of the ear to the temporalis and eyelids.',
'maxillary artery':'The bigger <b>terminal branch of the external carotid</b>. It passes through the <b>alar canal</b> and ends as the infraorbital artery.',
'occipital artery':'A <b>dorsal</b> branch of the external carotid running toward the back of the skull (occipital area).',
'cranial laryngeal artery':'A branch to the <b>larynx</b>; it travels with the cranial laryngeal nerve.',
'lingual artery':'A branch of the external carotid into the <b>tongue</b>, running with the hypoglossal nerve.',
'facial artery':'A branch of the external carotid that crosses the <b>ventral border of the mandible</b> to the face and lips.',
'sublingual artery':'A branch off the facial artery running under the tongue to the <b>sublingual area</b>.',
'caudal auricular artery':'A branch of the external carotid to the <b>back of the ear</b>.',
'trigeminal (fifth cranial) nerve':'<b>CN V.</b> Its mandibular branch (V3) gives the lingual, inferior alveolar, mylohyoid and auriculotemporal nerves you see in this lab.',
'lingual nerve':'A V3 branch: <b>general sensation to the rostral 2/3 of the tongue</b>.',
'inferior alveolar nerve':'A V3 branch that enters the <b>mandibular foramen</b> and runs in the mandibular canal to the <b>lower teeth</b>. It exits the mental foramina.',
'mylohyoid nerve':'A V3 branch, motor to the <b>mylohyoideus</b> and rostral digastricus.',
'auriculotemporal nerve':'A V3 branch, sensory to the skin around the <b>ear and temple</b>; it rides with the facial nerve branches.',
'inferior alveolar artery':'A maxillary-artery branch entering the <b>mandibular foramen</b> with the inferior alveolar nerve to the lower teeth.',
'caudal deep temporal artery':'A maxillary-artery branch into the <b>temporalis</b> muscle.',
'middle meningeal artery':'A maxillary-artery branch into the skull to the <b>dura mater</b>.',
'external ophthalmic artery':'A maxillary-artery branch into the <b>orbit</b>, supplying the eye muscles and eyeball.',
'external ethmoidal artery':'Comes off the external ophthalmic artery toward the <b>ethmoid/nasal cavity</b>.',
'descending palatine artery':'A maxillary-artery branch in the pterygopalatine fossa. It splits into the <b>minor palatine, major palatine and sphenopalatine</b> arteries.',
'minor palatine artery':'A descending palatine branch to the <b>soft palate</b>.',
'major palatine artery':'A descending palatine branch through the palatine canal to the <b>hard palate</b>.',
'sphenopalatine artery':'A descending palatine branch through the <b>sphenopalatine foramen</b> into the nasal cavity.',
'infraorbital artery':'The <b>end of the maxillary artery</b>. It runs through the maxillary foramen and infraorbital canal with the infraorbital nerve and exits the infraorbital foramen.',
}
